    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15844" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">enthȳmēma</span></b> ,
			ătis, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθύμημα</span>, rhetor. and dialect. t. t. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A reflection</i>, <i>meditation</i>,
				<i>an argument</i> (pure Lat. commentatio), <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				10, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 14,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24</span></i>; 8, 5, 4
			et saep.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Top. 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			450</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A conclusion drawn from the contrary</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Top.
				13, 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 5, 9</span></i>.</div>
